  "period_note": "Year-end position from ONE Bank PLC's FY2025 Annual Report, Solo basis. Profit before tax was NEGATIVE (loss of 1,827.040m, driven by Total Provision of 6,465.126m against Total Operating Income of only 11,749.977m - Net Interest Income collapsed to 2,487.582m from 6,081.025m the prior year on rising cost of funds), but a large net deferred-tax income of 2,043.847m (current tax expense 556.344m offset by a deferred-tax credit of 2,600.190m) flipped this to a small positive Net Profit After Tax of 216.806m - the third consecutive year (2023, 2024, 2025 all show sharply declining or negative pre-tax profit rescued by deferred-tax credits, see insights.json) that reported PAT is dominated by tax accounting rather than operating performance. Same 'Five Years' Financial Highlights' PAT-anomaly caveat as FY2024 applies to this report's comparative columns for FY2020-2022 (this report simply reproduces the FY2024 report's exhibit for those columns unchanged). Balance-sheet finding: a new equity line 'Start-up Equity Investment Fund' (98.236m for FY2025, 96.068m for the FY2024 comparative) appears for the first time in this report; FY2024's OWN report had booked this fund within provisions/Other Liabilities (note 12.10 'Provision for Start up Fund'), not as equity - this exactly explains the entire difference between FY2024's own reported Total Shareholders' Equity (23,454.178m) and this report's restated FY2024 comparative (23,550.247m = 23,454.178m + 96.068m). A minor, fully-traced reclassification, not a profit or asset-quality restatement.",
